## Algorithm

Start the program.
Input the number of vertices and edges.
Create a graph using an adjacency list.
Input the edges representing friendships.
Accept the starting vertex.
Initialize all BFS levels to -1.
Set the starting vertex level to 0 and insert it into the queue.
Remove a vertex from the queue and display it.
Visit unvisited adjacent vertices, assign their levels, and insert them into the queue.
Repeat until the queue becomes empty.
Display the BFS traversal order.
Display reachable and unvisited vertices.
Count reachable vertices and display their BFS levels.
Stop the program.
